infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title PgBouncer pooling modes: ratio vs session state
  desc Session mode (left) vs transaction mode (right) — the ratio is the inverse of how long a client holds a real backend
  compares
    - label Session pooling
      children
        - label Session mode: backend per session
          desc Held minutes to hours of mostly-idle keep-alive
        - label Multiplexing about 1x
          desc Real backends roughly equal connected clients
        - label Session state stays safe
          desc Prepared statements, SET, LISTEN/NOTIFY, advisory locks all work
    - label Transaction pooling
      children
        - label Transaction mode: backend per transaction
          desc Held milliseconds, then returned to the pool
        - label Multiplexing 25 to 50x or more
          desc 1000 client connections collapse to about 25 real backends
        - label Session state breaks
          desc No server-side prepared statements, SET, LISTEN/NOTIFY, advisory locks
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
